## File Naming

```speclang
# @block:northstar/file-naming @kind:note
Specs support multiple formats:

.scl         → core speclang format
.spec.md     → markdown with mermaid, prose
.spec.yaml   → structured, machine-parsable
.go.spec     → direct mapping to .go file
.ts.spec     → direct mapping to .ts file

Core files: user writes .scl or .spec.md
Expanded: AI writes .spec.yaml
Direct: AI writes .{ext}.spec
Output: clean .go, .ts, .py, etc.

No fixed 1-10 levels. User sets max tokens/lines/chars.
Specs auto-split when over limits.
```

## Pipeline

```speclang
# @block:northstar/pipeline @kind:note
After convergence (no changes for 30s):

1. Read build.yaml
2. Run build commands
3. Run all generated tests
4. On success: commit, notify
5. On fail: rollback, notify, retry

Pipeline is self-defining in specs.
```

## Guard System

```speclang
# @block:northstar/guard @kind:note
Guard plugin enforces file ownership:

- Each agent session owns specific files
- Agents can read anything
- Agents can only write owned files
- Orchestrator has full access
- Users can create unguarded custom skills

Prevents agents from stepping on each other.
```

## Recovery

```speclang
# @block:northstar/recovery @kind:note
Self-healing on failure:

- Build fails → rollback spec, notify
- Test fails → rollback spec, show diff
- Agent timeout → kill, retry
- Max retries → pause, require human

Never leaves project in broken state.
```

